{"name":"Night Swim","hex":"#254a57","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"night","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is below the horizon when the sky is dark.","The period of darkness beginning at the end of evening astronomical twilight when the sun is 18 degrees below the horizon, and ending at the beginning of morning astronomical twilight."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Ellipsis of good night."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/night"},{"term":"swim","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move through the water, without touching the bottom; to propel oneself in water by natural means.","To become immersed in, or as if in, or flooded with, or as if with, a liquid."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act or instance of swimming.","The sound, or air bladder, of a fish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/swim"}],"entries":[{"title":"Night Swim","blocks":[{"text":"Night Swim is a 2024 American supernatural horror film written and directed by Bryce McGuire, and based on the 2014 short film by McGuire and Rod Blackhurst. Starring Wyatt Russell and Kerry Condon, it follows a suburban family who discover that their backyard swimming pool is haunted by a malevolent entity."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/15/Night_swim_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Swim","wikidata":"Q117842595"},{"title":"Night Swim (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Night Swim is the debut studio album by Australian singer-songwriter Josef Salvat. It was first released in France on 23 October 2015 by Columbia Records. An enhanced worldwide edition of the album was released on 19 February 2016."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/14/Josef_Salvat_-_Night_Swim.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Swim_(album)","wikidata":"Q24074909"},{"title":"Night","blocks":[{"text":"Night, or nighttime, is the period of darkness when the Sun is below the horizon. Daylight illuminates one side of Earth, leaving the other in darkness. The opposite of nighttime is daytime. Earth's rotation causes the appearance of sunrise and sunset. Moonlight, airglow, starlight, and light pollution dimly illuminate night. The duration of day, night, and twilight varies depending on the time of year and the observer's latitude."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/330px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night","wikidata":"Q575"},{"title":"Midnight blue","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight blue is a dark shade of blue named for its resemblance to the apparently blue color of a moonlit night sky around a full moon. Midnight blue is identifiably blue to the eye in sunlight or full-spectrum light, but can appear black under certain more limited spectra sometimes found in artificial lighting. It is similar to navy, which is also a dark blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg/330px-D%C3%BCsseldorf_Midnight_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_blue","wikidata":"Q947638"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Wyatt_Russell_on_Wizard_Radio_Media.jpg/330px-Wyatt_Russell_on_Wizard_Radio_Media.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Wyatt_Russell_on_Wizard_Radio_Media.jpg/330px-Wyatt_Russell_on_Wizard_Radio_Media.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikiped